Re-stamp an elastic RayCluster's templates on every write.

Kueue stamps the kueue.x-k8s.io/podset label and the slice name annotation on a
running elastic RayCluster's templates once, when it starts the cluster. A
re-apply of the manifest with kubectl apply, GitOps, or a JSON merge patch
replaces the atomic workerGroupSpecs list and drops both, so every worker
KubeRay creates afterwards stays gated forever, and a manifest without the
scheduling gate is rejected. Vanilla Kueue has the same defect.

The RayCluster defaulting webhook now also runs on updates. For an elastic
cluster it adds the scheduling gate to the head and worker templates, and, while
the cluster runs, sets each template's PodSet label and the slice name
annotation from the cluster's newest unfinished, unevicted Workload that holds
quota, so it never reads a finished or earlier chain's slice. The webhook
answers the write itself, so no second writer races the user's write, no pod is
deleted, and applying its own output again changes nothing. Clusters that are
not elastic are not touched. The mraycluster.kb.io rule gains the UPDATE
operation; deployments that install the release manifests or the upstream chart
add it themselves.

